* A single partition receives most of the traffic and causes consumer lag. How would you diagnose and fix the hot-partition problem?
* A consumer repeatedly joins and leaves its group, causing frequent rebalances. How would you identify and resolve the issue?
* Your producer's throughput is low even though the Kafka cluster has sufficient capacity. How would you investigate batching, compression, acknowledgments, and network latency?
* A consumer processes a message twice after restarting. How would you investigate offset commits and implement idempotent processing?
* Your business team wants to replay events from the last seven days. How would you configure retention and implement safe replay?
* A Kafka topic is growing rapidly and filling broker disks. How would you analyze retention settings and reduce storage pressure?
* A compacted topic is expected to retain the latest customer state, but consumers still encounter older records. How would you explain and verify compaction behavior?
* A broker restart causes producer errors and delayed message delivery. How would you distinguish expected leader-election delays from a cluster configuration problem?
* Your application uses a replication factor of three, but some partitions have fewer in-sync replicas than expected. How would you investigate the cause and protect data durability?
* A consumer cannot deserialize messages after a producer deployment changes the payload format. How would you restore compatibility without losing events?
* A team wants to increase a topic's partition count to improve throughput, but the application depends on key-based ordering. What risks would you evaluate before making the change?
* A new consumer deployment causes a large rebalance and a temporary processing outage. How would you minimize the impact of future deployments?
* A producer sends messages successfully, but a read_committed consumer cannot see them immediately. What transactional conditions could explain this behavior?
* Your Kafka cluster is healthy at the broker level, but end-to-end message latency is high. How would you trace latency across producers, brokers, and consumers?
